\item[* task:] The relation between Rs and S is before: PAST, but Rs 
has been `shifted' to the future expressed by the `future verb'.
               This rule is for a finite dependent clause.
               The `future verb' is incorporated into
the most left verb in the clause that gets a past future tense.
               The deixis 
value of the possible reference adverbial is checked for 
               future or omega
               The clause is marked for past superdeixis.
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
